        "language": "english",
        "review": "Visually influenced by the art deco vibes of  Bioshock, this anomaly spotting game provides  challenging anomalies, some almost invisible to the uninitiated player. The soundtrack can become somewhat grating, the vocals of the old-timey 1920s song can be annoying after a while. Something I did not love at all was the DON'T MOVE game mechanic, whenever the \"numbers station lady\" speaks. When you are almost at level 9 and you accidentally move your mouse, the frustration is insane.  No sir, didn't like it. Also a sore point: Its too damn dark! Even with the brightness turned up in the settings its still darker than the inside of a horse. Still very nice atmosphere, but could do without these things I mentioned.",
